  ],
  "regression_scope": "Existing rational shearing, automatic AMF/FT family seeds and target projection, root compilers, physical transport, cache and CLI all included in full release gate. Nine long scientific tests remain opt-in; no claim to rerun historical full benchmark systems.",
  "native_owners": [
    "Symbolica native root-polynomial grouping and AlgebraicQuotient inversion",
    "existing exact Gaussian rational epsilon valuations",
    "shared Frobenius integer constraints with Linnet graph storage",
    "existing DifferentialSystem::change_basis",
    "existing rational/algebraic physical transport, root-germ parity and prescribed contours",
    "existing cache identity/codec/range/error reindexing"
  ],
  "correctness_contracts": [
    "Extracted NormalizedRootEntry retains the prior compiler numerator/root parity algebra and inverse coefficient norm guards.",
    "Entry coefficients are normalized in the declared formal named-root quotient before Gaussian rational epsilon valuations; relation-hidden poles and cancellations are handled in this order.",
    "All partial derivatives contribute to one minimum valuation matrix; shared integer constraints and DifferentialSystem::change_basis implement I=diag(epsilon^weights) J and recheck nonnegative valuations.",
    "Original denominator occurrences, root radicands, quotient inverse norms and their generic epsilon leading coefficients are retained before cancellation or path specialization.",
    "Exact root declaration order, symbols and radicands are checked when converting identities; continuation metadata, root germs, normalization and original-domain conditions survive.",
    "Boundary conversions authenticate basis identities, check required source orders and reindex comparison errors without increasing verified precision; CLI emits original-basis output while keeping transformed cache identity.",
    "Native owners remain Symbolica polynomial grouping, Gaussian rational polynomials, AlgebraicQuotient inversion and matrix basis change; existing Linnet-backed integer constraints; shared physical transport and cache codec. No duplicate graph or tensor implementation was introduced."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "epsilon-dependent radicands rejected",
    "no nondiagonal epsilon regularization",
    "formal norm guards may exclude a point regular on one chosen sheet",
    "caller-supplied global original Laurent lower bound still required",
    "rectangular source coverage can be conservative",
    "formal root normalization can grow exponentially; no new root-count performance claim"
  ],
